          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What HbA1c target does guidance describe, and is there one number everybody uses?",
          "answer": "Guidance on HbA1c targets can vary between different organizations. Many guidelines suggest a target of 7 percent as a general standard, while others emphasize individualized targets tailored to each person's circumstances. Some guidelines may avoid stating a specific number to reduce the risk of rigid application in practice. Overall, the emphasis is on personalizing goals based on patient-specific factors rather than adhering to a one-size-fits-all approach. This information comes from the document titled \"Type 2 diabetes: glycemic targets and monitoring intervals.\"\n\nI could not cover specific numbers or recommendations from all possible guidelines, as there may be additional guidance from different health organizations that sets different targets.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
